# This is an EXUDYN example
#
# Details:  Flexible beams: Notebook `python/Notebooks/tutorialFlexibleBeams.ipynb`. Two simple planar beams and
#           the utility functions that build them: the `ObjectBeamGeometricallyExact2D`, a shear deformable
#           Reissner-Timoshenko beam, and the thin cable `ObjectANCFCable2D`, a large deformation Bernoulli-Euler
#           beam. Both beams are highly flexible, 2 m long, 5 mm high and 10 mm wide, made of steel. The shear
#           deformable beam is clamped to the ground, the cable is clamped to a moving ground. The outputs below
#           each cell are those of the last run.
